1 LIBRARY
    The LIBRARY command creates, changes, lists, and extracts from VAX/VMS
    libraries, in the style of VMS's LIBRARIAN: macro libraries (.MLB),
    which MACRO searches for macros, and object libraries (.OLB), which
    LINK searches for modules.  govax writes libraries as LIBRARIAN lays
    them out, so a library made here works on VMS, and VMS's work here.

    Syntax:

        LIBRARY <library>[/HOST] [<input>[,...][/HOST]] [qualifiers...]

    Parameters:

        <library>       The library file.  Without a file type it is .OLB,
                        .MLB with /MACRO, .TLB with /TEXT, or .HLB with
                        /HELP.  It can be a host file or a
                        file on a mounted volume, by the rules MACRO uses
                        for its source (see HELP MACRO).

        <input>         Files whose modules go into the library: macro
                        source (.MAR, the default type for a macro
                        library), one module for each macro, or object
                        files (.OBJ, the default for an object library),
                        one module for each object module, or shareable
                        images (.EXE, the default for a shareable image
                        library), one module each, holding the image's
                        name, ident, and universal symbols, or text files
                        (.TXT, the default for a text library), one module
                        each, of the file's records, named for the file or
                        by /MODULE=<name> after its name, or help files
                        (.HLP, the default for a help library), one module
                        for each level-1 key line ("1 KEY").  A bare name
                        is found beside the input before it.  With input
                        files and no operation named, their modules
                        replace any of the same names, as LIBRARIAN's
                        default /REPLACE does.

    Qualifiers:

        /CREATE[=(<option>:<n>,...)]
                        Creates a new library (a new version on a volume),
                        then inserts any input files' modules.  The options
                        are BLOCKS (which has no effect), GLOBALS, HISTORY,
                        KEYSIZE, and MODULES.

        /INSERT         Inserts the input files' modules.  A module
                        already in the library is a warning, and is left
                        as it is (in a text library, an error that ends
                        the command).

        /REPLACE        Replaces modules with the input files' ones of the
                        same names, inserting the rest.  The default.

        /DELETE=(<module>,...)
                        Deletes modules.  Names may hold the wildcards *
                        and %.  Deletions are done before any insertions.

        /EXTRACT=(<module>,...)
                        Copies modules out of the library, to the file
                        /OUTPUT= names (by default, the library's name
                        with the type .MAR, .OBJ, .TXT, or .HLP).  Names may
                        hold * and %.  /OUTPUT=SYS$OUTPUT shows a text,
                        macro, or help module.

        /LIST[=<file>]  Lists the library: its header, then its modules.
                        Without a file name, the listing goes to the
                        console; a file's default type is .LIS.

        /FULL           With /LIST, adds each module's ident, insertion
                        time, and number of global symbols.

        /NAMES          With /LIST, adds each object module's global
                        symbols.

        /WIDTH=<n>      The width of a /NAMES listing (80 on the console,
                        132 in a file).

        /MACRO          A macro library.  /OBJECT (the default) is an
                        object library, and /SHARE a shareable image
                        library, which LINK searches for the images that
                        define symbols (see HELP LINK), and /TEXT a text
                        library, which FORTRAN's INCLUDE reads (see HELP
                        FORTRAN), and /HELP a help library.  These choose a new library's type; an existing library keeps its
                        own.

        /NOSQUEEZE      Keeps macros' comments and trailing blanks.  By
                        default they're removed, as LIBRARIAN's /SQUEEZE
                        does, except on .MACRO, .ERROR, .WARN, .PRINT,
                        and .IIF lines.

        /SELECTIVE_SEARCH
                        Marks inserted object modules for selective
                        search: LINK takes from them only symbols already
                        referred to.

        /LOG            Reports each module inserted, replaced, or
                        deleted.

    LIBRARIAN changes a library in place; LIBRARY builds the whole library
    and writes it only when every step has succeeded, so an error leaves
    the library as it was; but a help file's bad key line, as on VMS, ends
    only that file's reading.  A changed library keeps its name and version,
    and no update history.  /COMPRESS and /DATA aren't implemented.

    From the host shell, "govax library <library> [<input>...]" runs this
    command, with --create, --insert, --replace, --delete, --extract,
    --output, --list, --list-file, --full, --names, --macro, --object,
    --share, --text, --no-squeeze, --selective-search, and --log.

    Examples:

        LIBRARY/CREATE/MACRO "mymacros" "mymacros.mar"
        MACRO "prog.mar"/LIBRARY=("mymacros")

        LIBRARY/CREATE DUA0:[LIB]SUBS SUB1,SUB2
        LINK MAIN,DUA0:[LIB]SUBS/LIBRARY

        LIBRARY/LIST/FULL/NAMES DUA0:[LIB]SUBS
        LIBRARY/EXTRACT=(ADD*)/OUTPUT="adds.mar" "mymacros.mlb"

        LIBRARY/CREATE/SHARE DUA0:[LIB]MYSHR SHR1.EXE,SHR2.EXE

        LIBRARY/CREATE/TEXT MYDEFS LIMITS.TXT,TIMES.TXT/MODULE=$TIMES
        DEFINE LNK$LIBRARY DUA0:[LIB]MYSHR.OLB
        LINK MAIN

    See also the help for MACRO and LINK.
